# Strip Tool-Appended Non-Schema Plan Sections

## Rule

After any `plan(operation="create")` call, read the generated file back and diff its
`^##` headers against the section schema the calling prompt mandates. Remove any section
the tool appended that the prompt does not list, before reporting success.

## Why

The plan-creation tool writes its own file template, which can include sections the
calling prompt explicitly forbids. When the prompt says "Non-schema sections are
forbidden" and the tool appends one anyway, the schema violation is in the artifact even
though the agent followed instructions. The read-back is the only place this is caught.

Observed: a `## Change History` section containing placeholder text
("_No revisions recorded yet_") was appended to every created plan, while the calling
prompt listed exactly ten permitted sections and named "Change History" as an example of
a forbidden extra.

## How to apply

1. Call `plan(operation="create", ...)`.
2. `grep -n "^## " <plan_file>` and compare against the prompt's required section list.
3. Delete any section not on that list, including its placeholder body.
4. Re-run the grep to confirm the header set now matches exactly, then report success.

Do not skip the read-back because the tool returned `status: success` — success means the
file was written, not that it matches the prompt's schema.

## Scope note

This is a verification step, not a fix to the tool. If the same non-schema section recurs
across sessions, the durable fix is to correct the plan-creation template at its source;
until then, the read-back-and-strip step is mandatory.
